    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is complete and all tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe requirement: when an owner is created (and read back), the API returns a `displayName` field formatted exactly as `LastName, FirstName` from the stored names.\n\nSince DTOs are generated from the OpenAPI spec via the openapi-generator plugin and populated by MapStruct, I made two changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `displayName` property (read-only string) to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` on `toOwnerDto` that computes the value via expression:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\",\n       expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")\n   OwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);\n   ```\n\nBecause `toOwnerDto` is the single mapping used by create, get, list, and page responses, `displayName` is now consistently derived as `LastName, FirstName` everywhere an owner is serialized. The acceptance test `coreComputesDisplayName` and the full suite are green.",
